.TH UBUNTU-DOCK-FOLDERS-XFCE 1 "October 2026" "Ubuntu Dock Folders"
.SH NAME
ubuntu-dock-folders-xfce \- manage application folders on the Xfce panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ubuntu-dock-folders-xfce enable
.RI [ --panel " ID" ]
.br
.B ubuntu-dock-folders-xfce disable
.SH DESCRIPTION
Enable or remove the Dock Folders panel plugin for the logged-in Xfce user.
Run it without sudo. The plugin selects X11 or Wayland when the panel starts.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B enable
Add the plugin to an Xfce panel, replacing its tasklist when one is present.
.TP
.B disable
Remove the plugin and restore its managed tasklist.
Folder settings are retained. This does not remove the Debian package.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --panel " ID"
Use the specified Xfce panel when enabling the plugin.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ubuntu-dock-folders (1)
.br
https://github.com/hawkab/ubuntu-dock-folders
